  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 5, 'WHO SMART Guidelines approach'. A 'Research and evidence base' bar feeds five knowledge layers, each with its product: L1 Narrative (enhanced guidelines), L2 Operational (digital adaptation kits), L3 Machine readable (machine-readable recommendations), L4 Executable (reference software) and L5 Dynamic (precision health models). Each layer passes through a 'Localisation' bar into a matching country-implementation adaptation: national policies and guidelines (L1), localised requirements (L2), localised machine-readable code and standards (L3), localised static digital services (L4) and dynamic digital applications optimised for local outcomes (L5). All five feed 'Data, evidence, and impact', which loops back to the evidence base as 'Evidence from digital implementations'.",
